,"\u002Fimages\u002F2011\u002F8\u002F13\u002F6810129.jpeg","https:\u002F\u002Fcalbears.com\u002Fimages\u002F2011\u002F8\u002F13\u002F6810129.jpeg",{"id":210,"title":115,"shortDisplay":115,"shortName":209,"abbrev":206,"facebookPage":-1,"globalSportGender":171,"globalSportId":208,"globalSportShortName":-1,"globalSportNameSlug":209,"instagramName":-1,"nonSport":-1,"pinterestName":-1,"ticketsLink":15,"twitterName":-1,"youtubeName":-1,"rosterId":15,"scheduleId":15,"displayOpponentHistory":-1},{"staff_title":4316,"staff_email":7947,"staff_phone":-1,"staff_twitter":4326},"blasquez@berkeley.edu",208,[8704,8705,8706,8707,8708,8709,8710,8711,8712,8713,8714],{"platformName":1020,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4364,"oldIcon":4365},{"platformName":1027,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4368,"oldIcon":4369},{"platformName":1014,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4372,"oldIcon":4373},{"platformName":4377,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4375,"oldIcon":4376},{"platformName":4381,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4379,"oldIcon":4380},{"platformName":4385,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4383,"oldIcon":4384},{"platformName":4389,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4387,"oldIcon":4388},{"platformName":4393,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4391,"oldIcon":4392},{"platformName":4397,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4395,"oldIcon":4396},{"platformName":4114,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4399,"oldIcon":4400},{"platformName":4404,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4402,"oldIcon":4403},{"id":8716,"title":8717,"firstName":8718,"lastName":8719,"image":8720,"sport":8725,"positionShort":-1,"call_to_action":-1,"bio":8726,"twitter":8727,"images":15,"displayFields":8728,"latestBioId":8716,"email":8729,"phone":21,"url":15,"staffId":8730,"socialMediaR":8731,"custom1":21,"custom2":21,"custom3":21,"custom4":21},1084,"Senior Director Of Football Affairs","Zac","Bocian",{"altText":8721,"url":8722,"absoluteUrl":8723,"creditName":15,"mediaCaption":15,"title":8724},"January 31, 2023; Berkeley, California, USA; California Golden Bears Media Day at Haas Pavilion; Zac Bocian (Photo credit: Kelley L Cox\u002FKLC fotos)","\u002Fimages\u002F2023\u002F2\u002F17\u002FZac_Bocian_20230131_103126_KCox_480x600.jpg","https:\u002F\u002Fcalbears.com\u002Fimages\u002F2023\u002F2\u002F17\u002FZac_Bocian_20230131_103126_KCox_480x600.jpg","2023 Cal Football Head Shot Zac Bocian",{"id":210,"title":115,"shortDisplay":115,"shortName":209,"abbrev":206,"facebookPage":-1,"globalSportGender":171,"globalSportId":208,"globalSportShortName":-1,"globalSportNameSlug":209,"instagramName":-1,"nonSport":-1,"pinterestName":-1,"ticketsLink":15,"twitterName":-1,"youtubeName":-1,"rosterId":15,"scheduleId":15,"displayOpponentHistory":-1},"Zac Bocian is in his seventh season at Cal and his fourth as Senior Director of Football Affairs after being promoted to the position on Jan. 12, 2022. Bocian's responsibilities at Cal are related to player personnel, football processes, strategic planning, recruiting, and roster management, among others. Bocian, who spent his first three campaigns at Cal (2019-21) as the team's Director of Player Personnel, will be working his 24th season in either the NFL or collegiate ranks in 2025.\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\n\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\nBocian is a native of nearby Pleasanton, Calif, and graduated from Cal in 2003. He and his wife, Noelle, currently reside in San Francisco with their daughter.\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\n\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\nBelow are additional notes on Bocian.\r\n\u003Cul>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Worked with the NFL's Cleveland Browns for 15 seasons (2003-17) including the final 13 in player personnel\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Served as the Western Region Scout for the 2019 Reese's Senior Bowl prior to his arrival at Cal\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Originally joined the Browns in 2003 and ascended from an intern in the video department to National Scout – Western Region\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Assisted in various scouting and coaching capacities throughout his tenure with the Browns\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>A tight end on the football team at Diablo Valley College before transferring to Berkeley\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Worked with the Cal football program as a student video assistant as an undergraduate in Berkeley\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\u003C\u002Ful>\r\n\u003Cstrong>Last Updated\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\nOctober 1, 2025\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\n ","ZacBocian",{"staff_title":4316,"staff_email":7947,"staff_phone":-1,"staff_twitter":4326},"zbocian@berkeley.edu",2998,[8732,8734,8735,8736,8737,8738,8739,8740,8741,8742,8743],{"platformName":1020,"userName":8727,"url":8733,"icon":4364,"oldIcon":4365},"https:\u002F\u002Ftwitter.com\u002FZacBocian",{"platformName":1027,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4368,"oldIcon":4369},{"platformName":1014,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4372,"oldIcon":4373},{"platformName":4377,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4375,"oldIcon":4376},{"platformName":4381,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4379,"oldIcon":4380},{"platformName":4385,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4383,"oldIcon":4384},{"platformName":4389,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4387,"oldIcon":4388},{"platformName":4393,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4391,"oldIcon":4392},{"platformName":4397,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4395,"oldIcon":4396},{"platformName":4114,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4399,"oldIcon":4400},{"platformName":4404,"userName":15,"url":15,"icon":4402,"oldIcon":4403},{"id":8745,"title":8746,"firstName":8747,"lastName":8748,"image":8749,"sport":8753,"positionShort":-1,"call_to_action":-1,"bio":8754,"twitter":8755,"images":15,"displayFields":8756,"latestBioId":8745,"email":8757,"phone":21,"url":15,"staffId":8758,"socialMediaR":8759,"custom1":21,"custom2":21,"custom3":21,"custom4":21},1074,"Assistant General Manager","Marshall","Cherrington",{"altText":8750,"url":8751,"absoluteUrl":8752,"creditName":7943,"mediaCaption":15,"title":8750},"2022 Cal Football Marshall Cherrington Head Shot","\u002Fimages\u002F2022\u002F8\u002F2\u002F480x600Marshall_Cherrington_Cal_FBC_20220623_165220_Al_Sermeno_411.jpg","https:\u002F\u002Fcalbears.com\u002Fimages\u002F2022\u002F8\u002F2\u002F480x600Marshall_Cherrington_Cal_FBC_20220623_165220_Al_Sermeno_411.jpg",{"id":210,"title":115,"shortDisplay":115,"shortName":209,"abbrev":206,"facebookPage":-1,"globalSportGender":171,"globalSportId":208,"globalSportShortName":-1,"globalSportNameSlug":209,"instagramName":-1,"nonSport":-1,"pinterestName":-1,"ticketsLink":15,"twitterName":-1,"youtubeName":-1,"rosterId":15,"scheduleId":15,"displayOpponentHistory":-1},"Marshall Cherrington is in his eighth season at Cal and his first as the Assistant General Manager in 2026. Cherrington's responsibilities in his new role include overseeing the personnel and recruiting departments, managing the revenue share cap and NIL efforts of the program and helping lead the program's creative direction and social media presence. Cherrington previously served as the Golden Bears' Director Of Player Persoennel (2022-25), Director of Recruiting Strategy (2019 - January 2021) and as a recruiting assistant (2018).\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\n\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\nCherrington graduated from USC in 2018 with a bachelor's degree in public relations with a business minor and emphasis in sports media studies.\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\n\u003Cbr \u002F>\r\nBelow are additional notes on Cherrington.\r\n\u003Cul>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Helped Cal sign a 2026 transfer portal class that ranked as high as No. 14 by 247Sports and a 2021 recruiting class that was ranked as high as No. 20 nationally according to ESPN \u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Produced content for Cal's recruiting social media platforms and also collaborated with Cal's Director of Recruiting to execute successful unofficial and official visits unique to each prospect.\u003C\u002Fli>\r\n\t\u003Cli>Has full-time professional experience at both USC as the Director of Recruiting Strategy (2021) and Washington as a player personnel analyst (spring 2019) after previously serving as a football operations intern at his alma mater 